# robonix/skill/p2pmov/move/status — poll the latest TBox task lifecycle.
#
# The TBox SDK reports ONE global task stream (SDK_BACK_TASK_STATU_T via
# the state callback); `run_id` is informational and empty means "the
# most recent task". The raw vendor task_state is mapped to a canonical
# state the executor's poller understands:
#   0 idle    -> PENDING
#   1 running -> RUNNING
#   2 success -> SUCCEEDED
#   3 paused  -> RUNNING   (not terminal — waiting for resume)
#   4 failed  -> FAILED
#   5 canceled-> CANCELED
string run_id
---
bool known          # false if no task status has been reported yet
string state        # PENDING | RUNNING | SUCCEEDED | FAILED | CANCELED | TIMEOUT
uint8 task_state    # raw vendor task_state (0..5, see above)
uint8 run_state     # raw vendor run_state (0 ready, 6 driving-to-goal, ...)
float64 distance_m  # remaining distance reported by the vendor, -1 if unknown
string detail       # human-readable
